{
 "credit": "LegendCraft \u2014 Berserker Reaver's Throw thrown-axe projectile (berserker.vfx.md 'Reaver's Throw'; rework doc bsk_thrown_axe row). BASE: exact vanilla iron-axe look \u2014 the thrown COPY of the held axe.",
 "comment_authoring": "Voxel extrusion of the CLASSIC (pre-1.14) iron_axe sprite, 1px=1u, 2u thick (thickness along X), UNROTATED and UNMIRRORED: model space = sprite space, square pixels, axe diagonal in its own frame \u2014 the way vanilla renders the extruded item. Haft runs down-left toward (-y,-z); the cutting edge's outward normal is diagonal (0, +1, -1)/sqrt2. A continuous tumble hides any fixed phase, so only STATIC poses (the lodged stand, the empowered flat spin plane) need the wiring to compose a 45deg roll constant.",
 "comment_pivot": "PIVOT/COLLISION = (8,8,8) = the axe THROAT (where the haft enters the head; sprite px 9.5,6.5) \u2014 RULED. The projectile seam puts the hitbox here and the flight spin rotates about it (server-side ItemDisplay transforms, spin axis X for the end-over-end tumble). Visual offset is ZERO by construction: any nonzero offset would orbit as the axe spins. Max visual sweep radius ~11u (~0.7 blocks at scale 1.0) \u2014 the blade edge orbits the hitbox by up to that much; accepted in the pivot ruling. BOTH models (base + empowered) share this pivot so the wiring swaps them freely.",
 "comment_no_animation": "NOTHING in this model animates. spin_arc/spin_flat/spin_return are plugin-side interpolated ItemDisplay transforms (setInterpolationDuration + setTransformation); the lodged stand pose is a static display transform.",
 "comment_flight": "Owner-signed flight constants (2026-08-14), DECLARED ONCE HERE. NB the sprite plane is Y-Z with thickness along X (not the vanilla generated-item X-Y convention) \u2014 the in-plane spin axis is model X. (1) All spins are IN the sprite plane about the pivot \u2014 the profile never goes edge-on mid-flight. (2) The CUTTING EDGE FACES INTO TRAVEL on every leg: outbound needs the mirror-facing yaw (the sprite's edge sits on the haft's -z side), the L60 return leg is the outbound literally reversed \u2014 opposite spin sense, same facing rule. (3) Spin sense: blade leads OVER THE TOP (forward tumble). (4) Cadence: 1 rotation per 5 ticks on the arcing throw; the empowered flat throw spins the same plane held horizontal at double rate. (5) Lodged stand: head buried to the cheek, haft trailing back toward the thrower at 35 deg off vertical.",
 "texture_size": [
  16,
  16
 ],
